> When the character is blind and wearing no gloves, how come (s)he doesn't
> get petrified when on an adjacent square to a cockatrice I press the 's'
> key for search? How is this different to feeling what's on the ground?

  Maybe since you're explicitly telling him to "search," he knows to
be cautious about it -- use a stick or a boot or something.  As opposed
to the reflexive action that happens when he moves onto a new space
and -- without thinking about it -- reaches down to feel what's touched
his foot...

> NH also shows that there is a corpse but doesn't tell what creature it was,
> which is OK. But why does NH also shows the correct color of the corpse even
> when blind, ie. yellow for cockatrice etc.

  This is a known "feature."  Also, potion colors are visible on the
screen from a great distance, even though the character can't tell what
they are until he walks over to them.

  One rationalization: Maybe when you're "blind", you're really just
kind of fuzzy-sighted; you can make out shapes and colors if you try
hard enough.  Except in the case of monsters, who don't stand still
long enough for you to make out their contours.
  Or maybe it would just be a real hassle to add to the Nethack
source code.  ( Blasphemy! :)

